{{- $debianLikeIDs := list "debian" "ubuntu" "pop" "linuxmint" "elementary" -}}
{{- if and (eq .chezmoi.os "linux") (has .chezmoi.osRelease.id $debianLikeIDs) (not .devpod) -}}
#!/usr/bin/env bash
# =============================================================================
# chezmoi run_onchange_after script: installs the current Profile's Linux
# (Debian/apt) Application list via `apt-get install`, reading the package
# list rendered by dot_config/empty_apt-packages.txt.tmpl from the Application
# list computed in .chezmoi.toml.tmpl. See
# docs/adr/0006-application-category-and-profile-manifests.md.
#
# `run_onchange_` (not `run_once_`) so editing the Profile's Application list
# and re-running `chezmoi apply` reaches an already-provisioned machine, not
# only a fresh install — the "applications" comment below is what changes
# the rendered script's content, and therefore its re-run hash, whenever the
# resolved list changes.
#
# `_after_` so this always runs once every Managed File — including the
# package list itself — has already been written. Unlike the macOS
# Application manifest, no Bootstrap-installed package manager is required
# first: apt ships with Debian/Ubuntu already.
#
# Debian/apt only, matching the Bootstrap script's own detect_linux_distro
# categorization (debian/ubuntu/pop/linuxmint/elementary) — this renders
# empty and never executes on Fedora/Arch/other distros, or on macOS/
# Windows, see docs/adr/0006-application-category-and-profile-manifests.md.
# Also excluded on devpod (a devpod container is always .chezmoi.os "linux",
# so it could otherwise match here) — devpod's Profile still carries GUI
# apps in its Application list, but a devcontainer shouldn't get them
# installed, matching .chezmoiignore's existing devpod GUI-config exclusion.
#
# Rerun trigger: hash of the rendered manifest, so a changed package
# identifier reruns this script too, not only a changed Application list.
# manifest sha256: {{ includeTemplate "dot_config/empty_apt-packages.txt.tmpl" . | sha256sum }}
# =============================================================================
set -euo pipefail

packages_file="$HOME/.config/apt-packages.txt"

echo "[INFO]  Installing Linux Applications via apt-get..."
sudo apt-get update -qq
xargs -a "$packages_file" -r sudo apt-get install -y -qq
echo "[OK]    Linux Applications installed."
{{- end -}}
